  "rules": [
    "Review only: nothing here is read by a catalog, generator, presenter or placement pool. godot/src/PropReskinTrial.cs builds the variants only inside its own capture scene.",
    "Shapes never change: each variant is the prop's own mesh. The swap re-projects UVs (object-space box projection, metres) and assigns the skin's own surfaces by role; the shader keeps the prop's own textures and remaps them.",
    "Swap surfaces are crops of the finished skin packs' existing atlases (godot/assets/shared-modules/concept-kit-v2/skins/<skin>/<role>_0.jpg base colour, _1.jpg glTF metallic-roughness, _2.jpg normal, and the authored local-colour emission PNG where a role has one). Rects are pixels in those 2048 x 2048 atlases.",
    "Roles follow the kit's material roles: stone (body), trim (frames, rims, dark wood), iron (metal) and glow (lantern glass).",
    "A prop may override its role mapping per skin (skins.<skin>: default, tops, rimTop, materials). tops sends every upward face to that role; rimTop only the upward faces near the prop's top.",
    "Captures stand each variant on the same free block (three cells clear toward the camera so no cut-away wall overlays it) under one identical neutral review fill light in every skin's room."
  ],
